+// Patch 0016, #125: edge cases found reviewing 0015. Expected values are literals. T0 is 2026-11-11 12:00:00 UTC.
+//
+//   1. A failing-notice claim only succeeds while the cursor still holds the last_success_at this invocation loaded.
+//   2. A name whose first get_profile fails (not for budget) gets a stub cursor: history_id '', page_token null,
+//      catch_up 0, last_success_at null, connection_id the resolved fingerprint, created_at now. A later poll of a stub
+//      calls get_profile; success sets history_id and last_success_at and clears failing_notice_at (no second row).
+//      While it keeps failing the abort rules apply with since = last_success_at ?? created_at. After 24 hours one item
+//      per streak says `Email watch could not start reading this account (trying since <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM UTC>)`.
+//   3. Migration 0023 adds created_at (tested in migration.test.ts); real cursors set it too; an abort measures from
+//      last_success_at ?? created_at ?? last_run_at.
+//   4. The sweep skips the cursor purge when the items purge fails with anything but a missing table.
+//   5. resolveConnection warns and restarts the name only when its guarded purge batch changed a row.
